### Summary of key design decisions

| Concern | Resolution |
|---|---|
| `copy_path` anchor | Called directly for all regular-file copies (top-level and in-tree). |
| Recursive symlinks | Recreated via `os.readlink` + `os.symlink`; never followed, including at the operand level. |
| Self-copy guard | `os.path.realpath` comparison before any filesystem mutation. |
| Existing dest directory | Bits preserved; new directories get `source_rwx & ~umask`. |
| Interactive / force | Delegated to `copy_path` for every regular file in the tree. |
| Resource limits | Depth cap 4096, node cap 10 000 000; both emit a diagnostic and stop. |
| Error continuation | Per-entry `try/except` in `_recurse`; top-level per-source `try/except` in `main`. |
| Unsupported types | Silently skipped in-tree; rejected at the top level with a diagnostic. |
